// THE EDITOR VIEW OF A TEAM (approved mockup 2026-11-21; Graph · Editor · Sequence): the files the agents write, as a code editor you watch. Every write, edit, read and command of the run is an event the serve recorded; `replay.ts` turns them into a schedule that is a pure function of the events,
// so the same run plays the same live and afterwards. The left is the project's whole file tree (any file opens, freely, like VS Code) with each file tinted by the agent that wrote it; the middle is the code, each agent a named pointer typing at human speed; the bottom panel has Terminal and Replay,
// the replay's controls sitting discreetly in the panel's tab bar. While agents work it is read-only; when they stop it is the real code editor and Ctrl/Cmd+S saves into the run's folder.
